  "name": "Capture LINE Receipt Expenses with Gemini and Verify Japanese Invoice Numbers",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "354874eb-9c10-4929-850d-2355f4e54ef8",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -160,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 1050,
        "content": "## Capture LINE Receipt Expenses with Gemini and Verify Japanese Invoice Numbers\n\nUsers send receipt images to a LINE official account. The workflow archives each image in Google Drive, extracts structured expense data with Gemini, checks Japanese Qualified Invoice Numbers against the National Tax Agency (NTA) Web-API for the receipt date, records valid expenses in Google Sheets, and replies in LINE. Non-image messages and invalid receipts receive guidance instead of being logged.\n\nWho's it for: finance teams, field sales staff, and Japanese businesses that want mobile receipt capture with invoice-status verification.\n\n### How it works\n1. A LINE webhook receives the message and extracts the message type, ID, reply token, and user ID.\n2. Non-image messages receive instructions for sending a receipt photo.\n3. Image messages are downloaded, archived in Google Drive, and converted to Base64.\n4. Gemini determines whether the image is a receipt and extracts the date, vendor, totals, category, description, and T-number.\n5. Invalid receipt images receive a retry message and are not added to the ledger.\n6. If a valid T-number is found, the NTA validity endpoint checks its status on the receipt date.\n7. The completed expense record is appended to Google Sheets and confirmed in LINE.\n\n### Setup\n1. Configure the LINE webhook and Channel Access Token header credentials for all LINE HTTP Request nodes.\n2. Configure a Gemini API-key header credential.\n3. Connect Google Drive and replace YOUR_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID with the archive folder.\n4. Connect Google Sheets and replace the spreadsheet and sheet placeholders. Create the columns listed in the Google Sheets node.\n5. Replace YOUR_NTA_APP_ID with your NTA Web-API application ID and add the production webhook URL in LINE Developers.\n\n### Customization tips\n- Adjust the Gemini categories, Google Sheets schema, or Japanese LINE messages to match your expense policy."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
